<A NAME=S8></A>
<H2>Summary</H2>
<UL>
<LI><CODE>Date</CODE> counts months from 0 and is a moment, not a day; clock changes and time zones can move
it to another day.<P>
<LI>Keep days as keys, <CODE>'2026-09-25'</CODE>: they sort and compare as text and save as they are. Keep
Date inside one module, at midday.<P>
<LI>Write tests first for fiddly code: the awkward cases (month ends, leap years) become part of the
program.<P>
<LI><CODE>JSON.stringify(value, replacer)</CODE> lets a function change what is written;
<CODE>Object.fromEntries</CODE> makes an object from <CODE>[name, value]</CODE> pairs.<P>
<LI><CODE>import * as X from './Module'</CODE> imports all a module's exports as one object;
<CODE>X[name]</CODE> chooses one by name.<P>
<LI>An object can be a lookup table: <CODE>{ a: 1, b: 2 }[key]</CODE>.<P>
<LI><CODE>Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) =&gt; ...)</CODE> makes an array of n items.<P>
<LI>The Toolbar makes a Draw-style toolbox with <CODE>side: 'left'</CODE>; buttons can be relabelled,
hidden and selected as the program's state changes.<P>
</UL>

